 chance of holding it. Mrvan has emphasized labor issues, including a bill penalizing companies that lock out workers, which fits the district's union-heavy profile.\n\nRepublican Barb Regnitz enters with a Trump endorsement and strong fundraising, and national GOP groups have signaled they will invest in flipping the seat. That makes this a genuinely contested race rather than a formality, but the structural lean and incumbent advantages still favor Mrvan clearly. No public general-election polling is available, so the forecast rests on fundamentals, ratings, and market pricing.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9569, "margin": 11.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9243, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9241, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9308, "margin": 9.5}]}